  "readmeFile": "README.NuGet.md",
  "releaseNotes": "12.1.1: the field under the on-screen keyboard is now lifted by the\n\t\t\tright amount. The lift was measured before the layout pass and came\n\t\t\tout random: on an 800x600 screen the digit pad covered half of the\n\t\t\tfield. Scrolling no longer moves the field out of its scroll area;\n\t\t\tthe rest of the lift pans the page.\n\t\t\t12.1.0:\n\t\t\tOn-screen keyboard: new looks next to the classic one, chosen with\n\t\t\tOnScreenKeyboardStyle.TextVariant / DigitVariant (both default to\n\t\t\tClassic, so nothing changes for an app that does not set them).\n\t\t\tLetters, Phone: shift and backspace at the ends of the third row,\n\t\t\tdigits and punctuation on a \"?123\" layer, a wide space bar, \"Done\"\n\t\t\tat the end of the bottom row, \"Undo changes\" in a strip above the\n\t\t\tkeys. Digits: Calculator (7-8-9 on top, a wide 0, the decimal\n\t\t\tseparator next to it, a tall \"Done\" on the right), TwoRows (two rows\n\t\t\tof five digits, the lowest pad) and Pad (4x4). The decimal separator\n\t\t\tfollows the culture; in whole-number fields its key stays in place\n\t\t\tdimmed. The strip shows the field name, its limits and the value\n\t\t\tbefore editing (OnScreenKeyboardField.Title / Hint); one-shot shift\n\t\t\tand auto-capitalised names (CapitalizeWords); the UI language first;\n\t\t\tthe full Russian alphabet. App-like colours, light and dark.",
